arbeitnow:director-gsi-alliances-emea-lo.description:
&lt;h4&gt;About Team &amp;amp; About Role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik&#39;s Alliances team works with the world&#39;s leading systems integrators to help hospitals, banks, governments and other critical organisations across EMEA keep operating through cyberattacks. As Director, GSI Alliances EMEA, you&#39;ll build and lead the regional GSI strategy from the ground up, turning partnerships with the biggest integrators into a repeatable engine for pipeline, services and cyber resilience outcomes. This is a rare chance to shape how Rubrik goes to market through GSIs across a whole region, with real ownership of the strategy and the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own Rubrik&#39;s EMEA GSI strategy, deciding which partners to prioritise and where to invest, so Rubrik is the data security platform integrators lead with in customer resilience programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build executive-level relationships with the regional and global leadership of our priority GSIs, creating joint plans that turn partnership into sourced and influenced pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Pre-Sales, Marketing and Specialist sales teams to align GSI engagement to key accounts, so customers get a joined-up Rubrik and partner experience from first conversation to deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale GSI service offerings, certifications and practices around Rubrik&#39;s platform, including data security, cyber recovery and identity resilience, so more customers can adopt faster with trusted delivery partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach and develop a high-performing GSI alliances team, creating clear paths for people to grow as the region scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the GSI forecast, business plans and quarterly reviews, using data to show what&#39;s working and where to double down&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Rubrik at partner events, customer briefings and industry forums, shaping how the market sees us in regulated sectors such as financial services, public sector and healthcare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with global Alliances and Product leadership to bring EMEA partner and customer insight into roadmap, programme and incentive decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Experience You&#39;ll Need&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience in alliances, partnerships or channel leadership within enterprise software, ideally cybersecurity, data protection, cloud or infrastructure, with a strong track record working with GSIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success building GSI relationships at senior level and turning them into measurable pipeline and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing teams, or leading through influence across Sales, Marketing and Services without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how GSIs make money (services attach, managed services, practice build-outs) and how to build joint value propositions around that&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and execute a regional strategy across multiple countries, cultures and regulatory environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and executive presence, comfortable with CxO-level conversations in both partner and customer settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial discipline: you plan, forecast and report with rigour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a GSI or alliances function in a high-growth or scaling company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with EMEA regulatory drivers such as DORA and NIS2 and how they shape cyber resilience buying&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with major GSIs and regional integrators across EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional European languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketplace and co-sell motions across the major hyperscalers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join Us in Securing and Accelerating the World&#39;s AI Transformation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik (NYSE: RBRK) is the Security and AI Operations Company, delivering one platform built at the intersection of data, identity, and AI. The platform enables agentic cyber resilience and trusted AI operations for enterprises worldwide, built to recover before disruption strikes and stay a step ahead, so security is never the reason ambition stalls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/rubrik-inc/mycompany/verification/&quot;&gt;Linkedin&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/rubrikinc&quot;&gt;X (formerly Twitter)&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/rubrikinc/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.rubrik.com&quot;&gt;Rubrik.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Inclusion @ Rubrik&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Rubrik, we are dedicated to fostering a culture where people from all backgrounds are valued, feel they belong, and believe they can succeed. Our commitment to inclusion is at the heart of our mission to secure the world’s data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to hire and promote the best talent, regardless of background. We continually review our hiring practices to ensure fairness and strive to create an environment where every employee has equal access to opportunities for growth and excellence. We believe in empowering everyone to bring their authentic selves to work and achieve their fullest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our inclusion strategy focuses on three core areas of our business and culture:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Our Company: We are committed to building a merit-based organization that offers equal access to growth and success for all employees globally. Your potential is limitless here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Culture: We strive to create an inclusive atmosphere where individuals from all backgrounds feel a strong sense of belonging, can thrive, and do their best work. Your contributions help us innovate and break boundaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;Our Communities: We are dedicated to expanding our engagement with the communities we operate in, creating opportunities for underrepresented talent and driving greater innovation for our clients. Your impact extends beyond Rubrik, contributing to safer and stronger communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/Disabled&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, protected veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable law. Rubrik provides equal employment opportunities to employees and applicants in all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, promotion, compensation, training, leave, and termination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rubrik provides reasonable accommodations to qualified applicants and employees with disabilities in accordance with applicable law. If you need an accommodation to participate in the application process or to perform your job, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ----- ----- Accommodations may include changes to the application process, documents in an alternate format, a sign language interpreter, or specialized equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO IS THE LAW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/olms/regs/compliance/eo_posters/employeerightsposter2page_19final.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;NOTIFICATION OF EMPLOYEE RIGHTS UNDER FEDERAL LABOR LAWS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

arbeitnow:product-manager-deal-lead-insu.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Pantheon has been at the forefront of private markets investing for more than 40 years, earning a reputation for an innovative approach to investing in secondaries, co-investments, and primary fund investments, as well as capital formation across commingled funds, evergreen vehicles and customized solutions. Our specialist investment capabilities span multiple strategies across private equity, infrastructure and real assets, and private credit. Through our collaborative and committed culture, we find new ways to solve complex problems together and deliver innovative investment opportunities across private markets. Pantheon currently manages approximately $82.3 billion in AUM across all its strategies, serving more than 750 institutional and 638 private wealth clients worldwide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For further details please visit &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.pantheon.com&quot;&gt;www.pantheon.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Manager / Deal Lead within the Global Insurance Structured Solutions team, within the Client Solutions Group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Role will work in close partnership with colleagues across the business, including the investment teams and global relationship managers, to develop, commercialise and execute new structured solutions and other products for insurers, asset managers, banks and others. The Role will also work with external parties within the insurance, asset management and structured solutions world, such as advisors, law firms, rating agencies, distributors, investors, brokers, regulators and others (“External Parties”), to create partnerships, appoint service providers, maintain market intelligence and know-how and develop new products and solutions for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will encompass several key areas (further and more complete details below):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product management “Deal Lead”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing management and servicing of existing products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New Product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counterparty Relationship coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investor-facing/RM support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GISS team strategy and agenda&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product management “Deal Lead”: leading structuring and management of launch process for new structured, insurance and other solutions (RFs, CFOs, bilateral CFOs, long-dated bonds, synthetic LPs etc, “Solutions”), in close coordination with Internal and External Parties, and managing more junior GISS colleagues involved in the product launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing management and servicing of existing Solutions: ongoing servicing of existing Solutions and support of investors, Relationship Managers and internal product management teams (CorePM, Fund Finance etc), for example, (i) developing the quarterly CFO monitoring and product management process in partnership with CorePM, Risk, Operations and Fund Finance, (ii) producing materials for investor meetings or other internal and external meetings and/or (iii) responding to internal or external questions about our business, services and Solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New Product Development – the research and development of new solutions and products. This will often be an iterative process involving ideation and development with External Parties (in any location) as well as internal colleagues such as other team members, investment teams, CSG colleagues, legal, operations, tax, compliance, CorePM and others (“Internal Parties”).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Counterparty Relationship coverage — maintaining and expanding our existing network across advisors, investors, distributors, rating agencies, law firms and other External Parties, including regular in-person meetings, informal market contact, conferences and other engagements (for the benefit of Solutions and investors in all locations).
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking primary responsibility for relationships with External Parties where assigned to the Role, but also involving other team members involved in those relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining involvement in relationships with External Parties where responsibility is assigned to another team member&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involvement of other GISS team members in such meetings and interactions for the benefit of the learning, development and relationship development of other team members, as well as for the purposes of innovation/ideation of new Solutions and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and aggregate market information, know-how, client needs, regulatory regimes, etc to help development of new ideas and to support execution of new solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investor-facing/RM support — supporting RMs at investor pitches and marketing meetings (both in person and remotely) as well as with ongoing relationship servicing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GISS team strategy and agenda.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the team head and the wider global GISS team, preserving global collaboration across the group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Representing the interests of the GISS team and the business as a leader within the GISS team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing junior team members, either direct reports, or other more junior team members who are not direct reports but with whom the Role is working on Solutions and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with the head of the GISS team, other Product Managers / Deal Leads and the broader GISS team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Note that responsibilities will need to be flexible to meet the needs of the GISS team, our stakeholders and the business more broadly, so these will likely evolve over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge and Experience Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in product development/management, investment solutions structuring and/or insurance solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of private markets, including secondaries, and across private credit, private equity, infrastructure and other private assets, and ideally also good knowledge of public debt markets, risk factors and dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with securitisations, collateralised fund obligations (“CFOs”) and rated feeder structures, including rating methodologies, modelling, structuring, investors, regulatory treatment, and other topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with market participants including rating agencies, lawyers, brokers, investors, asset managers and/or regulators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management and organisational skills with demonstrated aptitude for prioritisation and execution of complex projects and assigning and hitting deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of global insurance regulatory environments and the implications for both investment portfolio requirements and vehicle structures, including how to optimise for various client needs, especially capital treatment efficiency, liquidity and other objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing more junior staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legal knowledge/understanding and experience an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work well in a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This job description is not to be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements. You may be required to perform other job-related duties as reasonably requested by your manager.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pantheon is an Equal Opportunities employer, we are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce so if you&#39;re excited about this role but your past experience doesn&#39;t perfectly align we&#39;d still encourage you to apply.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

arbeitnow:enterprise-platform-engineer-e.description:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineer, Enterprise Platforms, you will be a hands-on owner of the collaboration tools our employees use all day. You will administer, automate, and improve them, working alongside identity, endpoints, and the wider SaaS stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who sees a problem, figures out the fix, and ships it. Our team is small and the scope is broad. You will have real ownership early, a lot of autonomy, and few layers between you and the people you support. You will turn policies, runbooks, and employee needs into reliable configurations, scripts, and self-service experiences. We use AI tools where they make us faster or more accurate, and we expect good judgment about when to trust them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reflects Abnormal VOICE values. You move with velocity, design for long-term ownership and governance, use data with intellectual honesty, stay close to customer needs, and aim for excellence in reliability and simplicity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer Google Workspace: users, groups, org units, shared drives, Drive sharing and DLP, Gmail routing and policies, Calendar and room resources, Meet, and audit and security investigation tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer Slack (Enterprise Grid): workspaces, channels, user groups, permissions, app approvals, Slack Connect, retention, export and eDiscovery, workflows, and audit logs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain automation for joiner, mover, and leaver flows, access requests, deprovisioning, and common employee needs, using SCIM, APIs, webhooks, Apps Script, and scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with identity (Okta SSO, MFA, group-based access) so Google and Slack access follows least privilege and birthright rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support endpoints and other SaaS platforms as needed, including macOS device management and long-tail SaaS administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create self-service experiences, runbooks, and enablement content so employees can resolve common needs without escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in Tier 2/3 incidents, perform root cause analysis, and feed what you learn back into automation, runbooks, and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add logging, dashboards, and reporting so changes are monitored and audit questions can be answered quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools where they help (documentation, troubleshooting, request triage, analysis), with human review and appropriate access controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security, GRC, Legal, People, Finance, and IT Service Delivery to deliver changes safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage incoming requests and incidents by impact and urgency, route them to the right owner or queue, and resolve or escalate within agreed response targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn vague or incomplete requests into clear requirements: ask clarifying questions, identify stakeholders and constraints, and confirm the desired outcome before building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear expectations with employees and stakeholders about scope, timelines, and tradeoffs. Give status updates proactively, and flag risks or delays early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce standards for external sharing, Slack Connect, guest access, and third-party and OAuth app approval in Google Workspace and Slack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run regular access and license reviews, using systems and audit logs to find unused, orphaned, or over-privileged access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep configuration baselines documented, changes tracked in ServiceNow, and evidence ready for SOC 2, ISO 27001, and FedRAMP audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review audit logs and investigate suspicious activity with Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document requirements, risks, and approvals for changes so they pass change review and can be audited later.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scripting and Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate first. If a task happens more than a couple of times, you script it, build a workflow, or turn it into self-service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write scripts and tools (Python, Apps Script, and shell) against the Google Workspace, Slack, and Okta APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations and workflows in Workato, connecting identity, HR, collaboration, ticketing, and SaaS systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Torii workflows to automate app discovery, onboarding and offboarding, and license reclamation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build ServiceNow catalog items and flows so requests are routed, approved, and fulfilled with minimal manual touch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep scripts and configuration in version control, with logging, error handling, and clear documentation so others can run and maintain them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Google Workspace, Slack (Enterprise Grid)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity:&lt;/strong&gt; Okta&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation and integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Workato, Torii, Python, Apps Script&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service management:&lt;/strong&gt; ServiceNow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Endpoints and other:&lt;/strong&gt; Jamf, Zoom, and a long tail of SaaS applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t need experience with every tool. Strong experience with comparable platforms, and a record of learning new ones quickly, is what matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation-first:&lt;/strong&gt; We remove repetitive work rather than absorbing it, and we measure success by manual touches eliminated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer-first:&lt;/strong&gt; Employees are our customers. We respond with urgency, communicate clearly, and fix root causes so the same problem doesn&#39;t come back. We do what we say we&#39;ll do, or we tell people early when that changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast-paced:&lt;/strong&gt; Priorities shift quickly and requests arrive from every direction. We move fast, ship in small steps, and iterate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time management and triage:&lt;/strong&gt; You juggle incidents, requests, and project work. You sort what comes in by impact and urgency, handle what&#39;s urgent first, and protect focused time for project work and for the root-cause fixes that prevent tomorrow&#39;s tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You find the problem before someone assigns it, and you follow through to a documented, working fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with ambiguity: unclear requirements, incomplete documentation, and shifting priorities don&#39;t stop you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You prioritize well when everything feels urgent. You set expectations early and honestly: you say no or &quot;not yet&quot; clearly and kindly, and you explain the reason.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You learn new platforms quickly and teach what you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You ask the right questions up front: who needs this, what problem it solves, what &#39;done&#39; looks like, and what could go wrong. You propose a recommended approach rather than waiting to be told.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate proactively: status updates, change notices, and honest post-incident write-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in IT engineering, systems administration, or a similar role supporting business-critical technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on administration of Google Workspace (Admin console, groups, Drive and sharing controls, Gmail, Calendar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on administration of Slack (workspace and channel management, user groups, app management, permissions). Enterprise Grid experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of identity and access concepts: SSO, MFA, least privilege, directory and group management, and SCIM or standards-based provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to script and integrate systems using APIs, webhooks, Apps Script, Python, or similar tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with incident and change management, troubleshooting, root cause analysis, and documented follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, including documenting technical processes and explaining complex systems to non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of working independently and taking ownership without close direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing scripts or building workflows that automate repetitive IT work, and a habit of automating before doing something manually a third time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-first approach to supporting employees: responsive, clear, and focused on fixing root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment and manage your time across incidents, requests, and project work, prioritizing by impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to set and manage expectations with stakeholders, including saying no or negotiating scope and timelines while keeping trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a startup or high-growth company, where you wore multiple hats, built processes from scratch, or scaled IT through rapid headcount growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with acquisitions, tenant or domain migrations, or workspace consolidation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data governance in collaboration tools: retention, legal hold, eDiscovery, DLP, and audit log analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google Workspace or Slack administration certifications, or involvement in their admin communities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Okta, Jamf, Zoom, or other enterprise SaaS administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in remote-first, SaaS-first, or zero-trust environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with version control, configuration-as-code, or CI/CD for platform automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building self-service workflows, or using AI tools to improve support, troubleshooting, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of security and compliance frameworks (SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP) as applied to collaboration and end-user platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Workato or a similar integration platform (Zapier, Tray.io, Boomi, or Okta Workflows).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Torii or another SaaS management platform, such as Zluri or BetterCloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ServiceNow (catalog items, flows, incident, request, and change) or a similar ITSM platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering Microsoft 365 (Entra ID, Exchange Online, Teams, SharePoint/OneDrive, or the M365 admin center), especially in a mixed Google and Microsoft environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-AA1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on AI in our process:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Abnormal AI uses AI-assisted tools to help our recruiting team prepare for candidate interviews. These tools analyze resume content and role requirements to suggest interview questions and areas for the interviewer to explore.They do not make hiring decisions or screen candidates automatically. Every decision about a candidacy is made by a person. Further, if your application is successful and Abnormal AI makes a conditional offer of employment, we will carry out pre-employment checks which must be successfully completed to progress to a final offer. All processes and pre-employment checks are in line with prevailing legislation and Abnormal AI&#39;s policies relevant to our security and privacy standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law. For our EEO policy statement please &lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt3a076cfd9753fa1f/blt9cbda641db7c0045/6a1e3d3a66aea075cd33e462/AAP_and_EEO_Statement.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;click here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. If you would like more information on your EEO rights under the law, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt3a076cfd9753fa1f/blt4eb3a265cc7b1ca9/6a1e3d3bfe33e73c16ff026b/EEOC_Know_Your_Rights_Oct_30_2025.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

arbeitnow:enterprise-account-executive-2.description:
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is looking for an Enterprise Account Executive to join the {Insert Region} team. This team sells our security solutions to Enterprise level accounts within a defined territory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate for the role will be local to the {Insert Location} area and have the following skillset:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hunt: disciplined approach to early pipeline development. Comfortable and have demonstrated ability to prospect into enterprise accounts with the ability to leverage/ balance five pillars of demand generation: AE prospecting, SDR, Marketing, Channel and Customer referrals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good qualifier: Ability to uncover / discover customer problems pains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good presenter: ability to present and demonstrate value based off customer pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disciplined in sales methodology / time management : Ability to systematically execute a disciplined sales process that can be repeated in parallel without sacrificing quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discipline in data integrity: Ability to continually maintain data accuracy and consistency for all accounts &amp;amp; opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and present a business case to a customer showing high ROI across different dimensions to multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to extract, document and organize lessons, knowledge and information about customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to guide internal stakeholders through their own internal buying processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grit; ability to find success in an early-stage environment without all the resources/teams available to much larger organizations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of how to leverage other departments including Sales Engineering, Marketing, BDRs, Product and Customer Success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell Abnormal AI solutions to your defined territory with the goal to overachieve new annual recurring revenue quota&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work enterprise accounts (&amp;gt;3k mailbox organizations) from initial conversations through signing a contract and up-selling once they’re a customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect and generate new business opportunities with enterprise accounts (&amp;gt;3k mailbox organizations) to supply enough pipeline for them to hit sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Customer success to ensure a timely renewal and expansion sale opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continually document results and maintain accurate data across all sales systems (Salesforce, Highspot, Close Plan)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a voice for the customer/prospect with internal teams including Sales Engineering/POV team, Product and Marketing to ensure appropriate prioritization to close more revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Haves&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise Account Hunter: Demonstrated 3+ years of direct (vs. overlay) enterprise experience prospecting, closing new logos and growing major accounts against incumbents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill in negotiating with large organizations and closing complex sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven performer with consistent over quota performance and/or top 5% of sales org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically competent: Conversant in key areas: security, email, cloud, AI, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cyber-security Software sales: Experience selling subscription software/SaaS to CISOs and security personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start-up experience: Success at a company that was early stage, underdog or was a new entrant with large competitors or similar (limited resources-build territory including: channel, tech partners, initial customer wins, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/BA degree or equivalent work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-RJ1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on AI in our process:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Abnormal AI uses AI-assisted tools to help our recruiting team prepare for candidate interviews. These tools analyze resume content and role requirements to suggest interview questions and areas for the interviewer to explore.They do not make hiring decisions or screen candidates automatically. Every decision about a candidacy is made by a person. Further, if your application is successful and Abnormal AI makes a conditional offer of employment, we will carry out pre-employment checks which must be successfully completed to progress to a final offer. All processes and pre-employment checks are in line with prevailing legislation and Abnormal AI&#39;s policies relevant to our security and privacy standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abnormal AI is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by law. For our EEO policy statement please &lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt3a076cfd9753fa1f/blt9cbda641db7c0045/6a1e3d3a66aea075cd33e462/AAP_and_EEO_Statement.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;click here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. If you would like more information on your EEO rights under the law, please&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://assets.contentstack.io/v3/assets/blt3a076cfd9753fa1f/blt4eb3a265cc7b1ca9/6a1e3d3bfe33e73c16ff026b/EEOC_Know_Your_Rights_Oct_30_2025.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

arbeitnow:senior-customer-success-manage.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;At Dragos, the mission is personal. The systems we protect deliver the water you drink, power your home, and keep the hospitals your community depends on running. Those critical infrastructure systems that power our civilization around the world are under attack every day by adversaries. When those systems fail, people are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;immediately&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;at risk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;We are the global leader in&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;xOT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;cybersecurity, combining technology, threat intelligence, and expert services. The people here chose this work because they understand&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;what is&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;at stake&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot;&gt;. Here, you will find a remote-first mission-driven team across North America, Europe, the Middle East, and APAC built on authenticity, transparency, and trust. If safeguarding the systems that protect your family, friends, and community is the kind of work that matters to you, you are in the right place.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP Selected SCXW107525881 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:120,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:360}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;As the Customer Success Manager (CSM) for EUROPE, you will serve as a trusted advisor to our industrial clients throughout their journey with Dragos. You’ll play a pivotal role in driving adoption, ensuring satisfaction, and aligning our solutions with the customer’s operational and security goals. You will be the bridge between Dragos and our customers, advocating for their success while aligning with internal teams to ensure world-class delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Serve as the primary post-sales point of contact for customers in the EUROPE region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Drive successful onboarding, implementation, and adoption of Dragos solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Partner with customers to define success criteria and help them achieve measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Conduct regular business reviews to assess value realization and identify expansion opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Act as the voice of the customer internally by relaying feedback to Product, Engineering, and Sales teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Manage renewals and support customer retention efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Sales, Professional Services, and Support to ensure a seamless customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Travel as needed across the region to build strong relationships and drive customer engagement (up to 30%).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Monitor and manage customer health metrics, identifying risks early and taking action to ensure account stability and satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Proactively manage and escalate issues as needed, including the development and execution of at-risk account recovery plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;5+ years of experience in Customer Success, Account Management, or similar roles in cybersecurity, enterprise SaaS, or industrial sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Familiarity with industrial control systems (ICS), OT security, or critical infrastructure environments is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Proven ability to manage complex customer relationships and influence key stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience working with EUROPE clients and understanding regional business practices and cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and relationship-building skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Comfortable working independently and across time zones in a remote-first environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Multilingual candidates, particularly those speaking German and other European languages, are highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Compensation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;3&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559683&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559684&amp;quot;:-2,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Salary: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;collapsed-field-text&quot;&gt;£85,000.00&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559683&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559684&amp;quot;:-2,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Competitive Equity Package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;4&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559683&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559684&amp;quot;:-2,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;2&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Comprehensive Benefits Plan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
