arbeitnow:director-corporate-communicati.description:
&lt;p&gt;Teneo is the global CEO advisory firm, working with the world’s leading companies to solve their most complex business challenges. We provide strategic counsel across communications, investor relations, financial transactions, restructuring, geopolitics, public affairs, management consulting, financial advisory, risk advisory and people advisory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With more than 50 offices worldwide, Teneo partners with CEOs, boards and senior executives to help organisations earn trust, navigate disruption and deliver against their strategic objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teneo is seeking a high-calibre Director to join our team in Berlin or Frankfurt. This is a senior, client-facing role with a focus on corporate communication and reputation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Director in Teneo Strategy &amp;amp; Communications business in Europe, you will be responsible for building trusted senior client relationships, leading complex client mandates in collaboration with (Senior) Managing Director and contributing to the growth and reputation of the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Berlin or Frankfurt, you will work closely with Teneo colleagues across Europe and the global network to deliver integrated advice to clients. This will include collaboration with specialists in corporate reputation, crisis preparedness and response, public affairs, geopolitics, management consulting, risk advisory, people advisory, sustainability, digital and creative campaigning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires both strategic advisory excellence and a strong commercial mindset. The successful candidate will be expected to bring market credibility, senior relationships, origination capability and the ability to lead multidisciplinary teams through complex, high-profile and often sensitive client situations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Client Counsel&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Act as trusted adviser to clients across a diversity of sectors and industries.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Provide leadership on corporate narrative, reputation, stakeholder engagement, issues management and crisis preparedness.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Advise clients on how to communicate effectively with employees, media, government, regulators, customers, investors, partners and other key stakeholders.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Bring judgement, discretion and confidence to high-pressure situations involving complex stakeholder dynamics, significant public scrutiny and reputational risk.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Corporate Communications and Crisis Situations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Develop communications strategies around major corporate events, business transformation, leadership change, restructuring, litigation, regulatory scrutiny, operational incidents, cyber incidents, activism and other significant or sensitive situations.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Advise clients on crisis preparedness, scenario planning, crisis governance, response strategies, messaging and stakeholder engagement.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Work closely with legal advisers, public affairs teams, risk specialists, management consultants and other advisers to ensure communications strategies are aligned with broader business objectives and stakeholder considerations.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Provide leadership in fast-moving and high-pressure situations involving intense scrutiny, competing stakeholder expectations and significant reputational risk.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Media, Reputation and Stakeholder Management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Develop and execute media strategies involving German, European and international business, corporate and national media.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Advise clients on reputation management, corporate positioning, proactive storytelling, executive positioning, crisis situations and complex issues.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Help organisations build and protect trust with their most important stakeholders through clear, credible and consistent communications.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Provide senior counsel on emerging reputational risks, stakeholder expectations and issues that may affect corporate licence to operate.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Leading project teams to develop and deliver communications that have real impact for our clients&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Providing team direction and management whilst acting as the day to day point of contact for clients&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Challenging the status quo with new thinking, new product development, and new ways of working&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Responsible for leading client servicing, profitability, forecasting and budgeting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Proactively contributing to and fostering the development of junior team members&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years’ experience of working in a senior role in corporate communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in an advisory firm is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience in managing project teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent understanding of media, social media, and stakeholder environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent ability to shape and deliver strategic advice to senior level clients&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage and mentor junior staff&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engaging self-starter with high attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptionally strong verbal and written communication skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborator who is able to foster good working relationships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time management and the ability to prioritise a varied workload&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable taking the lead on driving performance and revenue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native level German required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Teneo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teneo is the global CEO advisory firm. We partner with our clients globally to do great things for a better future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drawing upon our global team and expansive network of senior advisors, we provide advisory services across our five business segments on a stand-alone or fully integrated basis to help our clients solve complex business challenges. Our clients include a significant number of the Fortune 100 and FTSE 100, as well as other corporations, financial institutions, and organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our full range of advisory services includes strategic communications, investor relations, financial transactions and restructuring, management consulting, physical and cyber risk, organizational design, board and executive search, geopolitics and government affairs, corporate governance, ESG and DE&amp;amp;I.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The firm has more than 2,000 employees located in 50+ offices around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

