arbeitnow:senior-category-lead-modern-ar.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Catawiki, every day brings the extraordinary! Whether it’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/583-sports-memorabilia&quot;&gt;Daniel Ricciardo’s Formula 1 Car&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/579-fossils&quot;&gt;Woolly Mammoth’s Skeleton&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/l/10035805&quot;&gt;Lady Gaga&#39;s Jumpsuit&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/583-sports-memorabilia&quot;&gt;Usain Bolt’s running shoe&lt;/a&gt;, we encounter exceptional objects every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a one-of-a-kind marketplace for buying and selling special objects. Each week, more than 100,000 unique items are auctioned, all carefully curated by our passionate in-house experts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Having sold over 25 million unique objects, our mission is to become the world’s most popular destination for special objects. As a growing, diverse and sustainable scale-up, we proudly live by three core values. If these values resonate with you, we’d love to explore how you can join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking ownership and driving impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being open to change and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being passionate about our mission and our customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Special objects are the final frontier of e-commerce. As Senior Category Lead for Art – Primary Market, you’ll bring structure and consistency to the team’s day-to-day work. You’ll turn priorities into clear plans, strengthen how work moves across the team, and help each person take ownership of outcomes. Alongside this operational focus, you’ll support the Senior Category Manager in translating the category vision into practical initiatives that improve the experience for buyers and sellers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll create an engaged team culture built on trust, clear expectations, and accountability, helping people build on their strengths and grow in their roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll also coordinate with Sales, Marketing, and other relevant teams to deliver cross-functional improvements and keep the category’s priorities moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create a clear operating rhythm:&lt;/strong&gt; Turn category priorities into practical plans with clear owners, milestones, and regular follow-up so work moves forward reliably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve day-to-day operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Clarify workflows and handovers, spot bottlenecks early, and help the team resolve blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build team ownership and accountability:&lt;/strong&gt; Set clear goals and expectations, coach team members to take responsibility for their work, and help them use their strengths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen engagement and development:&lt;/strong&gt; Hold regular 1:1s, give timely feedback, and support each person’s growth in partnership with the Senior Category Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use performance insights to guide action:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor category results, identify risks and opportunities, and coordinate focused actions with relevant teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate strategy into delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Senior Category Manager’s vision by coordinating cross-functional initiatives from planning through execution and review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify category growth opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt; Use market and performance insight to spot where the category can grow, then work with relevant teams to turn promising opportunities into practical initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; You have a strong track record of creating structure, setting priorities, and ensuring reliable execution in a category, sales, or commercial team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team leadership and coaching:&lt;/strong&gt; You help colleagues perform at their best through clear goals, regular feedback, coaching, and support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership and accountability:&lt;/strong&gt; You set clear expectations, follow through on commitments, and encourage others to take responsibility for outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organised project delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; You coordinate cross-functional work, manage dependencies and timelines, and keep stakeholders aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical judgment:&lt;/strong&gt; You use data and customer or market insight to identify issues, set priorities, and evaluate results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear, constructive communication:&lt;/strong&gt; You build trust, share context, give direct feedback, and adapt your communication to different stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interest in contemporary art:&lt;/strong&gt; You bring a genuine interest in contemporary art and the primary art market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work in the Art Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re a supportive, friendly Art team&lt;/strong&gt; that works together to tackle ambitious growth challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll work across Art – Primary Market&lt;/strong&gt;, supporting the Direct from the Artist and Photography categories with clear day-to-day priorities and coordinated delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll collaborate with Sales, Marketing, HR, and relevant partner teams&lt;/strong&gt;, agreeing owners and next steps so decisions turn into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll report to the Senior Category Manager in Art – Primary Market&lt;/strong&gt; and take part in the Art cluster’s management discussions, sharing updates, aligning on priorities, and raising blockers early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll be&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferably this role is hybrid,&amp;nbsp; based in Amsterdam. You’ll work from our Amsterdam HQ at least two days per week.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;text text-align-left &quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love Working with Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create a visible impact &lt;/strong&gt;by working at scale in a global organisation serving millions of customers across 80+ categories. In our flat structure, every role has a broad scope and directly impacts both our customers and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn and grow&lt;/strong&gt; through our Learning &amp;amp; Development initiatives, including clear development plans and mentorship programmes to support your career progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A culture of connection defines us&lt;/strong&gt;. We’re a passionate, diverse team of 800+ Catawikians representing 60+ nationalities. We foster an inclusive and queer-friendly environment where everyone is encouraged to bring their full self to work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Celebrate life’s moments with us. &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll receive a €100 Catavoucher when you join, a €50 Catavoucher on your birthday, and an extra day off each year to “Pursue Your Passion&lt;strong&gt;”&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer additional leave for key work anniversaries and important life events. Benefits may vary by location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Offices and Way of Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Our vibrant offices in Amsterdam and Lisbon are designed to inspire collaboration. Most Catawikians operate in a hybrid setup, combining office-based and remote work, with a minimum of two days per week in the office, unless a role is explicitly stated as fully remote or fully office-based.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interested?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Apply with an English CV and Cover Letter. By applying, you agree to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/conditions/applicant-privacy-policy.pdf&quot;&gt;Catawiki’s Applicant Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support the review of your application. AI may help us assess how your experience matches the requirements of the role, but hiring decisions are always made by our recruitment team&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

arbeitnow:director-corporate-issues-cris.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Burson, part of WPP, is the global communications leader built to create value for clients through reputation. With highly specialized teams, industry-leading technologies and breakthrough creative, we help brands and businesses redefine reputation as a competitive advantage so they can lead today and into the future. When you work at Burson, you are part of a global community of lifelong learners who thrive at the edge of innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WPP (LSE/NYSE: WPP) is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel in a single company – powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open, to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;WPP.com&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/&quot;&gt;bursonglobal.com&lt;/a&gt; and follow us on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/burson/posts/?feedView=all&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/burson.global/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More about the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Director within our Corporate, Issues &amp;amp; Crisis team, you will be a senior strategic advisor and team leader – protecting and enhancing the reputations of some of the world’s most significant organisations. Based in Amsterdam, you’ll lead high-stakes issues and crisis work across the Energy &amp;amp; Industrials, Healthcare or Technology sectors, counselling senior clients through their most sensitive moments and delivering media training that builds their confidence and capability. You’ll grow existing relationships, win new business, and help build the visibility, reputation and talent of the team in the Netherlands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a leading role in developing Burson’s corporate, issues and crisis work in the Netherlands – retaining existing clients and growing new business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted advisor and senior counsel to clients, adding strategic value during sensitive, high-stakes and reputational moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead issues and crisis programmes for clients across the Energy &amp;amp; Industrials, Healthcare or Technology sectors, anticipating risks and building proactive response plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver media training and crisis simulation exercises that build client confidence and capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the visibility and reputation of the team – with a view to winning new business and attracting talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor client teams, nurturing talent and contributing to a strong, collaborative team culture across the agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take responsibility for budget monitoring, revenue forecasting, resourcing and fee negotiation to ensure the correct level of profitability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Burson externally in relevant specialist forums, network groups and speaker platforms across the Dutch and EU market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience that contributes to success:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven background leading corporate, issues and crisis management within both agency and in-house settings, with strong exposure to complex, high-stakes scenarios and strategic media relations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sector expertise across either Energy &amp;amp; Industrials, Healthcare or Technology with a strong understanding of the issues shaping these industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in designing and delivering media training and crisis simulation exercises, alongside wider reputation management initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in managing communications across a broad range of stakeholders – including media, government, employees, investors and consumers – during sensitive, high-pressure moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially driven and entrepreneurial, with a track record of independently identifying and converting new business and managing client relationships end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trusted advisor to senior communications leaders and C-suite executives, with excellent interpersonal skills and credibility at the highest levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong, collaborative team leader, experienced in resourcing, commercial oversight and building high-performing, resilient teams, with previous experience within both agency and client-side environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full professional proficiency in Dutch and English, with the confidence to counsel clients and present in both languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-RE1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You belong at Burson:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is for Burson to be the leading ‘academy company’ for creative communications professionals and emerging leaders. We provide a dynamic environment where ambitious colleagues come to elevate their skills, expand their networks, and ultimately, produce the best solutions for today’s leading brands. Our commitment to your growth is reflected in our robust benefits and people programs, which include professional development opportunities, mentorship programs with industry leaders, a vibrant and inclusive company culture fostering collaboration and innovation and packages designed to reward and retain top talent. We invest in our people because we believe their success is our success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Burson, we’re an agency of learn-it-alls. We recognize that the things we do best, creativity and communications, require a level of nuanced understanding. That’s why it’s imperative for us to hire extraordinarily talented people of all backgrounds and identities. Without that we can’t do the essential work of inspiring bold ideas, fostering constructive dialogue, cultivating meaningful experiences, and driving innovation and creativity for our partners. Your unique point of view—your talent—is what makes you a #BursonPerson, and it’s how we deliver exceptional results for our clients, together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you click the &quot;Submit Application&quot; button below, this will send any information you add below to Burson. Before you do this, we think it&#39;s a good idea to read through our &amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy. &lt;/a&gt;California residents should read our  &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bursonglobal.com/p/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice. &lt;/a&gt;This explains what we do with your personal data when you apply for a role with us, and, how you can update the information you have provided us with or how to remove it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

arbeitnow:senior-director-head-of-qualit.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Head of Quality &lt;span style=&quot;font-size: inherit;&quot;&gt;&amp;amp; Responsible Person&lt;/span&gt; for Encaleret, International, leads the quality organization of BridgeBio Pharma Europe B.V. and reports to Senior Vice President Quality. As the Responsible Person, the role carries personal accountability under EU GDP for the entity&#39;s distribution activities: release for distribution, recalls, and products that are authentic, correctly stored and transported, and traceable. The role is independent of Commercial Operations, Manufacturing and Supply Chain, with an unrestricted right of escalation to the entity&#39;s full board. She/he leads and develops the entity&#39;s quality team, maintains the entity&#39;s quality management system, developed with the affiliate quality leads from existing BridgeBio frameworks, and leads WDA licensing, inspection readiness and subsequent MIA readiness, if needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the named Responsible Person on the WDA: release for distribution, recall decisions, and GDP compliance of the entity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take final disposition decision on returned, rejected, recalled or potentially falsified products (an RP decision under GDP), in consultation with BridgeBio&#39;s Global Quality Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and coordinate returns, rejections, suspected falsified products and recall operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approve return to saleable stock&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that customers are entitled to receive the products prior to shipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the WDA registration remains current with the commercial supply chain setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the accuracy of quality records and that GDP requirements are implemented and maintained in the quality management system, as required for the WDA license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the WDA application and IGJ inspection readiness&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data integrity and own the entity&#39;s internal audit (self-inspection) program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the GDP quality agreement matrix: contract service providers, 3PLs, distributors and intercompany interfaces&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and write standard operating procedures in BridgeBio’s document management system in accordance with the GDP requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure there is a training program for BridgeBio staff working under GDP and ensure that the relevant staff members are trained on GDP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in GDP vendor qualification program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality review of assigned quality events such as deviations, change controls, supplier notifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform distribution release for finished goods received from the contract manufacturing organization, which can include review of temperature, shipping and receiving documentation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for and be directly involved in product complaints from the EU and ROW markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide GDP and QA related support and intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be available and reachable 24/7&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other QA/Quality Person related responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and develop the entity&#39;s quality team: deputy RP, QA compliance/QMS, and QA operations/GDP; and QP, if needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain the entity&#39;s GDP-compliant quality management system by adopting existing BridgeBio quality frameworks, adapted to the entity&#39;s license requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the affiliate quality leads to resolve quality issues and keep the intercompany interfaces effective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare subsequent MIA readiness (QP recruitment, import, API GMP verification, and batch-certification processes), if needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in updating CMC sections of regulatory and quality documents as needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in regulatory inspections&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in internal and external project team meetings&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and review governing procedure (e.g., SOPs, WIs, etc.), where necessary&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You’ll Work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a Netherlands-based role that will require 30% travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in pharmaceutical quality, including significant GDP / distribution quality experience; prior appointment as (or eligibility to be) a Responsible Person strongly preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory inspections with EU competent authorities (IGJ preferred)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience of managing third party vendors (CMOs, CTLs, 3PLs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior relevant knowledge and experience related to the distribution of medical products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of supply chain concepts, supplier management, inventory&amp;nbsp;management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of US/EU GMPs /GDPs and associated guidance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working in a highly regulated environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership of quality teams; experience building quality functions or systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS degree preferably in operations, science, pharmacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documented GDP training and the education and experience to be accepted as Responsible Person by the Dutch authorities (Farmatec/IGJ)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Skills&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding the EU and particularly IGJ regulations in relation to the wholesale distribution of medicines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English language; written/spoken in Dutch language, preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong planning and time management skills with ability to prioritize workload&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with keen attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of data concepts and enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems e.g., SAP&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ready to embrace company core values and diverse corporate culture&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Rewarding Those Who Make the Mission Possible&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have high expectations for our team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market leading compensationHybrid work model - we value your flexibility in how you work, but encourage time in the office to strengthen our culture, collaboration, and sense of community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We provide career development through regular feedback, continuous education and professional development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate strong performance with financial rewards, peer-to-peer recognition, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
